  "method": "Every round (R4, R2) is at least the 1.5 mm wall, so with T the drafted box (half-widths 40 - z tan1 and 25 - z tan1, 0 <= z <= 10), P = T without its top and bottom with the walls pushed in by 4, Pi = P + 2B and G = Pi n {z <= 8}: the body is K = (G + 2B) n {z >= 0} and the cavity C = (G + 0.5B) n {z >= 0} (walls in by 1.5, rounds 2.5 and 0.5, top at 8.5). A section of G + sB at z <= 8 is the rectangle of the walls pushed in by 2 - s with four corners cut by the ellipse of the inclined corner cylinder of radius 2 + s (semi-axes Rl along the diagonal and R across, l = sqrt(1 + 2 tan^2 1)): area 4AB - 4D, D = c(c - y1) - R^2 l atan(1/l), c = R sqrt((l^2+1)/2), y1 = R (l^2-1)/sqrt(2(l^2+1)), integrated in closed form. Above z = 8 the section is the set within s of G, its boundary found in each direction from the exact distance to G (the projection on the side wall where it lies at or below z = 8, the top face, or the rim's rectangle with elliptic corners), integrated over z = 8 + s sin(phi) by Gauss-Legendre. The same code with no draft gives the closed form by Pappus (V = plan h - (1-pi/4) rho^2 L - 2 pi ((R-rho) + rho/(6(1-pi/4))) (1-pi/4) rho^2) to 2e-11. V(K) = 39431.151846, V(C) = 30546.856313, V = 8884.295533 mm3 (converged to 3e-10). Faces: the body's 18 less the bottom, their 17 inner copies and the bottom's rim, 35",
